stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: Controller state transitions and cycle accounting
  accDescr: Synchronous active-low reset takes any state to IDLE. Start is accepted only in IDLE or DONE. CLEAR and CAPTURE each last one cycle. COMPUTE runs steps zero through T minus one. DONE persists until another start. Busy cycles increment cycle_count to T plus two.
  direction LR

  state "IDLE<br/>busy = 0; done = 0<br/>hold while !start" as IDLE
  state "CLEAR<br/>busy = 1; clear = 1<br/>1 cycle" as CLEAR
  state "COMPUTE<br/>busy = 1; en = 1<br/>step = 0 … T − 1" as COMPUTE
  state "CAPTURE<br/>busy = 1; capture = 1<br/>1 cycle" as CAPTURE
  state "DONE<br/>busy = 0; done = 1<br/>hold while !start<br/>cycle_count = T + 2" as DONE

  [*] --> IDLE: synchronous reset
  IDLE --> IDLE
  IDLE --> CLEAR: start
  CLEAR --> COMPUTE
  COMPUTE --> COMPUTE: step != T − 1
  COMPUTE --> CAPTURE: step == T − 1
  CAPTURE --> DONE
  DONE --> DONE
  DONE --> CLEAR: start

  note left of IDLE
    Any state + !rst_n at rising clk:
    IDLE; step = 0; cycle_count = 0
    Unlisted control outputs = 0
  end note
  note left of COMPUTE
    T = K + 2N − 2 = 10 (N = K = 4)
    start ignored while busy
    step increments on self-loop; 0 elsewhere
    Accepted start zeroes cycle_count
    Each busy edge increments cycle_count
    cycle_count holds 12 in DONE
  end note
